ThreeInstructors←{
⍝ '' if uwsch reads an instructor list split over three lines ('A,' 'B,' 'C') the
⍝ way the reference model does. Made from fixture ⍵ by adding a third name after
⍝ a two-instructor cell that is already split over two lines.
    t←⍵
    m←⊃{⍵/⍨','∊¨⍵}∪⊃,/{⍵.classes.instructor}¨RefParse t
    a b←Trim¨','(≠⊆⊢)m
    e←{⍵/⍨{∨/(a,',',⍵,b)⍷t}¨⍵}(CR LF)(,LF)(,CR)    ⍝ the line break between the names
    0=≢e:'no split two-instructor cell in this fixture'
    p←a,',',(⊃e),b
    t←(p⎕R(p,',',(⊃e),'Third Person')⍠('Regex' 0)('Mode' 'D'))t
    exp←⊃,/{⍵.classes.instructor}¨RefParse t
    0=+/∨/¨'Third Person'∘⍷¨exp:'test setup failed: third name not added'
    exp Diff2 ⊃,/{⍵.classes.instructor}¨⊃##.uwsch t
}
